 ## Lessons learned
 - See `.ai/lessons.md`.
+- On this Windows/Git-Bash workstation, the ARCHIFY_HOME resolution one-liner from
+  `archify-setup.md` (`node -p '...split(require("path").sep).join("/")'`) is itself
+  corrupted by MSYS's automatic argument path-conversion: the literal `"/"` inside the `-p`
+  string gets rewritten to the Git-for-Windows install path (`C:/Program Files/Git`) before
+  Node ever sees it, producing a garbage homedir string. Fix: export `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`
+  (or `MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*'`) before any `node -p`/`node -e` call that embeds path
+  separators as string literals. See `.ai/docs-setup-step.md` for the measured before/after.
 
